{"event_type":"llm_call","call_index":6,"timestamp":44.35879876317219,"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a deep research assistant. You MUST conduct thorough investigations using web search and visit tools before providing any answer.\n\n# RESPONSE STYLE\n- Keep your final answer as brief and concise as possible\n- Avoid lengthy explanations - be direct and to the point\n- Focus on key facts and findings without unnecessary elaboration\n\n# CRITICAL RULES\n- You MUST search and visit web pages BEFORE giving any answer\n- NEVER provide an answer without first using search and visit tools\n- Always gather real data from the web, do not rely on your training knowledge alone\n\n# RESEARCH STRATEGY\n1. Search first: Use 2-3 search queries to find relevant sources\n2. Visit extensively: Visit 8-15 pages MINIMUM to gather comprehensive information\n3. Batch visits: Always visit 4-6 URLs in a single visit call for efficiency\n4. Search returns ONLY titles and URLs - NO content/snippets\n5. Synthesize: ONLY after gathering enough information from web sources, provide your answer within <answer></answer> tags\n\n# CRITICAL: SEARCH RESULTS ARE MINIMAL\n- Search tool returns ONLY page titles and URLs\n- Search results contain NO content, NO snippets, NO summaries\n- You MUST use visit to see actual page content\n- Without visiting pages, you have ZERO information about content\n- More visits = better research quality (aim for 10+ page visits)\n\n# EFFICIENCY TIPS\n- Combine multiple queries in a single search call\n- Visit multiple URLs in a single visit call (visit 4-6 URLs at once is optimal)\n- Visit diverse sources to cross-verify information\n- Don't repeat visits to the same URL\n\n# URL RULES\n- ONLY visit URLs from search results. Never invent URLs.\n- Use the visit tool to get detailed page content when snippets are insufficient.\n\n# Tools\n\nYou may call one or more functions to assist with the user query.\n\n<tools>\n{\"type\": \"function\", \"function\